      "name": "Military, defense & geopolitics",
      "items": [
        {
          "headline": "Xi says AI must stay \"under human control\" at the White House; Trump says he wants to leave AI rules where they are",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "The Hill", "url": "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/6109283-xi-china-us-ai-responsibility-trump/" },
            { "name": "CNBC", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/24/trump-xi-meeting-china-washington.html" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "Speaking in the White House Grand Foyer on 24 September, Xi Jinping said: \"We have both the capability and responsibility to develop and manage AI for good and ensure that the development of AI is always under human control and serves the well-being of the people.\"",
            "Earlier the same day Trump wrote on Truth Social that AI would be a \"big topic of discussion, but I want to leave it exactly where it is\", adding: \"That is China's position also. Our guardrail is the DOJ.\"",
            "CNBC reports Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the two countries agreed to extend their temporary trade truce — which lowered US tariffs and suspended Beijing's rare-earth and critical-mineral export controls — by two months from mid-November to January 10.",
            "Neither leader announced a binding AI agreement. This follows the first US-China AI talks reported in an earlier edition; what the notification mechanism discussed by both sides would actually cover has not been published."
          ],
          "topics": ["china", "us-federal-policy"],
          "impact": "neutral",
